WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.370
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.790
<i>Studying out in a café!</i>

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.360
<i>I'm practically a Tokyoite already!</i>

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:15.160
<i>I doubt anyone would even guess
a gal like me came out here from Okayama.</i>

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.620
Oh, excuse me.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.560
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, I'm sorry!

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.710
I'll just get my things together and clear out right away!

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:22.500
Wait...

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.620
Makoto-san?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.750
Yup. It's so close to home
so it doesn't take any time getting here.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.080
Are you working?

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.140
Yeah. I got assigned to a new client

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.440
but I have no idea what they even make, so I've been looking them up.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.770
I'll get those orders in just you wait!

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.950
Do keep your voice down if you could.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.860
Okay then, I better get back to work.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.030
Right! Hope I didn't bother you!

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.290
<i>Makoto-san is so cool!</i>

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.290
<i>Is it just me or does she seem down though...?</i>

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:31.700
Here's your S size caffè latte.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.160
That's not mine.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.460
I didn't order that either.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.540
Oh, uhh...

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:41.550
Sorry for the mix up, one S sized caffè mocha.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.770
<i>Something seemed a little off with Makoto-san...</i>

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.190
<i>Wait, don't tell me...!</i>

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.650
Oh great... How am I going
to stay focused with her here?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.070
<i>Oh, I am just the worst!</i>

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.290
<i>I know!</i>

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.070
<i>She likes all sorts of sweets, right?</i>

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:01.750
I'm home!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.580
Welcome!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.080
Michiru, what's going on here?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.370
Thank you for dropping by Café Michiru!

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.500
We've got just the sort of drinks you might like!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.750
Like Coffee Rum, the coffee liqueur!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.960
Brought to you right from
the home of coffee itself in Mexico!

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.090
Coffee Rum! This is one of my favorite drinks!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.090
But what's with this whole getup?

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:25.640
I just felt bad for bothering you at work today.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.850
So this is my way of saying sorry.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.980
But you didn't bother me at all.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.980
I should really be thanking you, actually.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.150
Wait, what?

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.110
I was sure I had thrown your whole day off or something.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.790
Oh no, not at all.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.410
Mind if I still indulge in a donut, though?

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:43.750
Be my guest!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.910
I'm glad you like all this though.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.370
Something just seemed off about you back at the café.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:59.630
It's just your regular sort of work problems.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.790
What about you?
Make any progress with your prep work?

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.390
Wha?! Oh, well, yes, sort of...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.100
'Kay, let me fix us up something to drink.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.930
We'll start off with some ice in the glass
and add one part of this Coffee Rum.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:16.160
Then we'll pour in three parts of some nice cold milk.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.440
And with just a little stir...

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.360
There you have it! A Coffee Rum ice latte!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.410
Here's to a hard day's work, today.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.080
And here's to you.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.410
Cheers!

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.290
That rich sweet flavor washes right through the body...

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:40.000
It has that mild creamy flavor,
with just a hint of alcohol behind it...

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.920
A shining example of a dessert cocktail!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.640
It really caught me off guard the first time I had some.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:49.260
I was expecting alcohol,
but it was more like a drinkable dessert.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.560
I still fall back on Coffee Rum whenever
I want to relax but don't want anything too strong.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.080
Milk-based cocktails have a really
comforting taste that's perfect for that, huh?

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.360
And it's just way too easy to drink!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.700
While I've got you here Makoto-san.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.990
Do you know what other ways
you can drink Coffee Rum?

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:12.900
I looked up a bunch of great recipes
I can whip up just for you!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.500
Here's your menu!

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.790
Thanks...

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.460
<i>You're showing it to me upside down though...</i>

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.210
Okay then,

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:25.050
I'll take a Coffee Rum Cola.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.220
Coming right up!

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.230
Michiru have you ever worked
in the food industry before?

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:35.100
Huh?

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.230
N-no...

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.110
Done like a pro!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:48.250
So we start with a glass of ice and add in
one part Coffee Rum and three parts cola.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.870
Mix it up just a tad.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.660
And there you have it!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.620
<i>I was supposed to be the one making that...!</i>

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.120
How does it taste?

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.920
The cola is sweet and rounds out the taste.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:09.090
And that slightly bitter coffee flavor that follows it is great.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:12.390
The Coffee Rum really blends in well
to give it a nice, rich taste!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.700
And it's not too bubbly or anything either.
Definitely an easy to drink cocktail.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:19.100
I'm gonna make something else!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.860
This here sounds good too.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.400
Coffee Rum ice tea!

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.740
Just straight unsweetened tea,
mixed with one part Coffee Rum to four parts tea.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.030
Does that make it coffee? Or tea?

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.750
It tastes like both!

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:39.290
It tastes like a syrup sweetened ice tea at first,
but a hint of black coffee follows it right up.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.290
So it's not really either, but...

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.630
They really complement each other
in a totally drinkable way!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.850
The perfect drink to go with dessert!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.010
I know it's pretty late already,
but let's enjoy it just this once...!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.390
It probably wouldn't be half bad mixed with some juice.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.810
This is the perfect sort of drink
for getting adventurous while drinking at home!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:07.570
Okay Makoto-san, what'll you have next?

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.740
Would you mind hearing me out on something first?

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.330
S-sure what is it?

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.290
SMILE!

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:15.950
Bwha?!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.450
I smile too fake, they said!

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:23.200
I've spent the past three years working at that café
and no one ever made even a single remark!

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:24.960
So why now all of a sudden?!

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.910
Okay, so what happened exactly?

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.470
I did an internship thing as part of my job search.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.220
I-I'm Makoto Kiriyama.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.970
You shouldn't fake a smile like that.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.240
I'm guessing you've never worked
in front of customers before?

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.980
Just thinking about it is infuriating!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.150
So I spent all day at work worrying over how I was smiling,

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.980
and it was awful cause I couldn't focus at all.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.490
Worst day ever.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.660
So that's what that was all about...

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.660
I don't wanna grow up anymore...

00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:00.020
You'll be fine! Even I'm managing!
You'll adjust in no time!

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:04.540
You work in sales, right Michiru?
What kind of face do you put on all day?!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.250
Uhh, well...

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.130
Something like this...?

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.380
That's the most forced smile I've ever seen.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.280
Because you're forcing me!

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.040
The polar opposite of cute...

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.890
Not even the slightest bit huh...?

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:25.500
Gah, now I can't even remember
what kind of face I normally put on...

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.650
I'm home!

00:08:26.660 --> 00:08:27.900
Nao-san!

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.450
Nao-san works floor sales,
so she must be a customer relations pro!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.320
I bet she can give us some tips!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.410
I'm not a fan of the idea but she's our only hope!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.660
Nao-san!
Sis!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:41.370
Hmm? Oh, my! What is it you two cuties?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.660
She reeks of booze...

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.420
She definitely had a few before coming home...

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.670
So this is the kind of face she puts on, is it?

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.330
Ah, Coffee Rum!

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:56.340
Two cuties drinking just the cutest of drinks, huh?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.600
Hey, Nao-san?

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.310
What sort of face do you put on
when you're dealing with customers at work?

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:04.060
Just the same face as always!

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:08.160
Thanks for shopping with us!

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.770
Really...?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.450
One caffé latte please!

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.500
C-coming right up!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.290
Michiru?

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.080
Back again!

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.580
You've got a new item on the menu starting today right?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:28.380
I've tried this one out, myself. It's really good.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.340
It goes really well with our coffee, if I do say so myself!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.960
Makoto-san!

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.840
That face right now was the most perfect smile!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:36.910
What...?

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:39.450
Looks like you don't have anything
to worry about after all!

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:43.160
You must have just been nervous at your interview.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:49.360
Don't go comparing a one-off thing at some other place to all the years you've spent working here!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.820
Just have some confidence, Makoto-san!

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:53.370
Someone waiting on a caffé latte?

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:55.270
Huh? O-oh, that's me!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.290
Wait Michiru! Your dessert!

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.540
Whoops!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.250
Just be yourself when you smile!

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.250
'Kay!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.410
It's so gooood!

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.730
<i>The key to a nice smile is just relaxing!</i>

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:22.040
<i>Treat yourself to a coffee and a nice dessert and chill out!</i>

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:24.520
Wait! I'm not getting any work done!

00:11:55.580 --> 00:12:02.530
Coffee Rum is a distilled liquor made
from sugarcane blended together with Arabica coffee.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:06.200
It's great not only in cocktails
but also as an ingredient in some snacks.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.870
I think I might use some to make some coffee jelly.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.750
Here's to another night!
